{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "toolbar",
  "title": "Project Panel Toolbar",
  "navigationLabel": "Project Panel Toolbar",
  "summary": "Tools for adding projects, sorting, filtering, and switching views.",
  "manualPath": "/user-manual?section=toolbar",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "toolbar-001",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Project Panel Toolbar"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-002",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The toolbar at the top of the project panel provides controls to add projects, adjust the sort order, filters, view modes, and docking side. Hover each element in the demo below to see its interactive state."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-003",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use the titlebar's Help button for the manual, Tutorial to replay the project tour, and × to collapse the panel. Reopening it retains the current search, filters, and view mode during the session. Closest To Me sorting needs your current location; Closest To Pin needs a location selected with the map search first."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-004",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Add Project"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-005",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Opens the project creation form so you can add a new dataset entry to the atlas. You must be logged in to use this button; if you are not, a prompt will appear asking you to sign in first."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-006",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Sort"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-007",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Opens a dropdown to choose the project ordering: "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Newest First"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ","
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Oldest First"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Closest To Me"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", or"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Closest To Pin"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Click Apply to confirm the selection or Clear to reset to default order."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-008",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Filter"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-009",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Open Filter to choose a category (River, Watershed, Places, Other), custom tags, and favorites. The menu opens over the panel and map so its options remain visible near panel edges. It follows the Filter button when the panel moves or scrolls, fits the viewport, and scrolls internally when space is limited. Select Apply to confirm or Clear to reset all filters. An active filter turns the button amber and adds a badge showing the number of active filters."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-010",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Favorites in Filter"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-011",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Open Filter, select Show only favorited projects, then Apply. Combine favorites with category and tags. Clear resets all filters. Click outside the menu or press Escape to close without applying pending changes; Escape returns focus to Filter. Login is required for the favorites option."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-012",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "View Scope"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-013",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Switches between showing "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "All"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " from the database or only projects whose location falls within the "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "current map viewport"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". When \"In View\" is active the project count in the info bar updates as you pan and zoom the map."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-014",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Grid / List View"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-015",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Switches the project panel between "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "grid view"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " (project tiles laid out in a grid) and "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "list view"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " (compact rows showing just the title and action buttons). The icon shows the mode you will switch"
        },
        {
          "type": "em",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "to"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " when clicked. The button is highlighted when list view is active. List view is fixed at 310 pixels wide and cannot be resized. Grid view restores its adjustable width. When Projects and GIS both dock on the left, list view is used automatically. The bordered, square-cornered list area joins the toolbar and keeps rows inside the panel, including during hover movement. Hover a row for about half a second to see its project tile preview toward the map: to the left of a right-docked panel, or to the right of a left-docked panel. Moving off the row dismisses it; very narrow spaces may hide the preview."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-016",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Move Panel"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-017",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Moves the project panel to the opposite side of the screen. Click once to dock it on the left, click again to move it back to the right. This is useful for keeping the panel out of the way of areas of the map you want to inspect."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-018",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Project Search Bar"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-019",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Type a keyword and press "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Enter"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " or click the search button to search for projects by title. Click the"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "×"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " button to clear the search and return to the normal project listing. While a search is active the map viewport filter is temporarily suspended."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-020",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Project Count Info Bar"
        }
      ],
      "role": "feature-title"
    },
    {
      "id": "toolbar-021",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Shows the total number of projects currently displayed after all active filters are applied, along with a label indicating the scope (\"all projects\" or \"in view\"). The count updates in real time as you apply filters, search, or pan the map."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
